WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.970
Community sporting clubs are asked to hold a working-with-children check for every volunteer.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.220
Now they’re also scored on how those checks are administered.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.820
A new poster asks what that score is really tracking.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.800
Its authors followed forty-eight clubs, from three sporting codes,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.508
through three audit rounds in one season.

00:00:21.308 --> 00:00:23.648
We gave every club a tier at each round,

00:00:24.048 --> 00:00:28.078
on a five-level maturity model that runs from Ad Hoc to Assured.

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:31.688
Here are four of those clubs, round by round.

00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:34.098
Club A rose from Level two to Level four,

00:00:34.198 --> 00:00:35.008
then fell back.

00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:36.408
Club D did the reverse.

00:00:37.208 --> 00:00:39.978
A club’s tier tracked the days left until its next audit,

00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:42.453
with a correlation of point seven one.

00:00:42.753 --> 00:00:46.033
No independent record of its onboarding practice came as close.

00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:49.573
It’s a pattern we keep rediscovering.

00:00:49.873 --> 00:00:55.771
An instrument built to certify practice tends to end up certifying the moment it was checked.

00:00:56.571 --> 00:00:58.781
Finals eligibility is tied to the top tier.

00:00:59.081 --> 00:01:04.751
Clubs below Level four when a round began were two point six times more likely to drop a marginal volunteer

00:01:04.851 --> 00:01:06.471
from the roster within a fortnight.

00:01:07.271 --> 00:01:10.321
We never told twelve of the clubs when their audit was due.

00:01:10.621 --> 00:01:12.271
Their tiers churned all the same.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:15.461
The tier is set by something about the assessment window itself.

00:01:16.461 --> 00:01:21.971
A tier that rises before an audit and settles after it is not measuring the club.

00:01:22.271 --> 00:01:23.851
It is measuring the audit.
